.Dd July 31, 2026
.Dt LANDSTRIP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm landstrip
.Nd run a command inside an OS-level sandbox
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -debug
.Cm run
.Op Fl -trap-fd Ar fd
.Op Fl p Ar file | Fl -policy Ar file
.Op Fl -policy-format Ar format
.Fl -
.Ar program
.Op Ar argument ...
.Nm
.Op Fl -debug
.Cm policy Cm validate | Cm resolve
.Op Fl p Ar file | Fl -policy Ar file
.Op Fl -policy-format Ar format
.Op Fl -tool Ar program
.Nm
.Op Fl -debug
.Cm doctor
.Nm
.Op Fl -debug
.Cm windows Cm install
.Op Fl -restricted-accounts Ar count
.Op Fl -unrestricted-accounts Ar count
.Op Fl -proxy-port-range Ar low-high
.Nm
.Op Fl -debug
.Cm windows Cm status | Cm uninstall
.Nm
.Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
loads one or more policies, applies the current platform sandbox, and runs a
program.
The
.Fl -
separator before the program is required.
.Pp
Policies use the supported subset of the Anthropic Sandbox Runtime format.
JSON is the default; YAML is also accepted.
Unknown fields are ignored.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "policy validate"
.It Cm run
Run a program under the merged file and executable policy.
.It Cm policy validate
Check policy parsing, path resolution, executable policy, and current platform
support without starting a program.
.It Cm policy resolve
Print the normalized merged policy as JSON.
.It Cm doctor
Print a JSON report showing whether the current platform sandbox is usable.
.It Cm windows install
Install and activate restricted-user isolation.
This command requests elevation.
The default installation creates eight restricted-network accounts, two
unrestricted-network accounts, and permits proxy ports 60080 through 60111.
.It Cm windows status
Print the active Windows implementation and its health as JSON.
.It Cm windows uninstall
Remove restricted-user isolation and return to AppContainer.
.El
.Pp
The
.Cm windows
command family exists only in Windows builds.
AppContainer is used when restricted-user isolation is not installed.
An unhealthy installation is an error and never causes silent fallback.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -debug
Enable debug logging.
.It Fl p Ar file , Fl -policy Ar file
Read a policy file.
This option may be repeated.
Use
.Sq -
to read standard input; it may appear once and requires
.Fl -policy-format .
.It Fl -policy-format Ar format
Set the format to
.Va json
or
.Va yaml .
The default for files is
.Va json .
.It Fl -tool Ar program
For
.Cm policy validate
or
.Cm policy resolve ,
include policy attached to the resolved executable.
.It Fl -trap-fd Ar fd
On Unix builds, write structured traps to an already-open descriptor numbered 3
or higher.
.It Fl -restricted-accounts Ar count
Set the restricted-network Windows account pool size.
The default is 8.
.It Fl -unrestricted-accounts Ar count
Set the unrestricted-network Windows account pool size.
The default is 2.
.It Fl -proxy-port-range Ar low-high
Set the inclusive loopback proxy range for restricted Windows accounts.
The default is 60080-60111.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print version information and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage information and exit.
.El
.Sh POLICY
Later policy files are merged over earlier files.
Objects merge recursively, arrays are combined without duplicates, and scalar
values replace earlier values.
Executable policy is merged last.
.Pp
The accepted fields are:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "filesystem": {
    "allowWrite": ["."],
    "denyWrite": ["**/.env"],
    "denyRead": ["~/.ssh"],
    "allowRead": ["~/.ssh/config"]
  },
  "network": {
    "allowNetwork": false,
    "httpProxyPort": 8080,
    "socksProxyPort": 8081,
    "allowLocalBinding": false,
    "allowUnixSockets": ["/run/user/1000/agent.sock"],
    "allowAllUnixSockets": false
  },
  "windows": {
    "appContainerMode": "lpac",
    "allowLoopback": false
  }
}
.Ed
.Pp
YAML path fields may be lists or newline-separated strings.
Relative paths are resolved from the directory where
.Nm
started.
.Sq ~
and
.Sq ~/
resolve to the current user's home directory.
Path entries accept
.Sq * ,
.Sq ** ,
.Sq ? ,
and character-class globs.
.Pp
On Unix, supplementary executable policy is read from the
.Va user.landstrip.policy
extended attribute.
On Windows it is read from the
.Va landstrip.policy
NTFS alternate data stream.
The executable is resolved through
.Ev PATH
and canonicalized first.
.Ss Filesystem
Writes are denied by default.
.Va allowWrite
grants writable roots and
.Va denyWrite
always takes precedence.
Reads remain unrestricted while
.Va denyRead
is empty.
Once it contains an entry, reads use an allowlist and
.Va allowRead
adds exceptions.
The most specific read rule wins.
.Pp
Concrete
.Va denyWrite
paths are enforced on all platforms.
Glob denies are matched at access time on Linux and macOS, including for files
created after sandbox setup.
Windows does not enforce glob
.Va denyWrite
entries.
.Ss Network
Direct TCP connections and new Unix sockets are denied by default.
.Va httpProxyPort
and
.Va socksProxyPort
allow loopback connections to those ports.
.Nm
does not start a proxy, set proxy environment variables, or filter domains;
the caller must do so.
.Pp
.Va allowLocalBinding
permits local TCP binding and connections to loopback addresses.
Windows rejects this setting.
On macOS, the Seatbelt localhost matcher may also include addresses assigned to
other local interfaces.
.Va allowUnixSockets
allows pathname Unix sockets, while
.Va allowAllUnixSockets
allows all new Unix sockets.
Unix socket policy is unsupported on Windows.
.Pp
.Va allowNetwork
set to true disables Landstrip network enforcement but leaves the filesystem
policy active.
.Ss Windows
Windows requires an explicit read allowlist; a policy with unrestricted reads
is rejected.
The removed
.Va windows.backend
field is also rejected.
Use the
.Cm windows
commands to select restricted-user isolation.
.Pp
.Va windows.appContainerMode
selects
.Va lpac
or
.Va standard .
LPAC is the default and the stronger boundary.
Standard AppContainer can also see resources granted to
.Va ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES .
.Va windows.allowLoopback
is an AppContainer-only opt-in that exposes every local loopback service, not a
single proxy port.
.Pp
AppContainer cannot enforce individual proxy ports.
With
.Va allowNetwork
false and no loopback exemption, it has no network access.
Restricted-user isolation permits only proxy ports in the range selected at
installation and rejects
.Va windows.allowLoopback .
.Sh PLATFORM NOTES
.Bl -tag -width Windows
.It Linux
Landlock enforces filesystem roots.
A seccomp broker handles policy operations Landlock cannot express, network
address checks, and per-access query traps.
.It macOS
Seatbelt enforces filesystem and network rules from a profile fixed at process
startup.
.It Windows
AppContainer or restricted local users enforce explicit filesystem grants.
Restricted-user mode uses account-scoped Windows Filtering Platform rules.
Per-run grants are removed after the process tree exits.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
.Cm policy validate ,
.Cm policy resolve ,
.Cm doctor ,
and Windows management commands each write one JSON document to standard
output.
An invalid validation report has
.Va valid
set to false and includes stable
.Va code
and
.Va message
fields.
Operational failures remain traps rather than validation reports.
.Pp
Landstrip failures and broker-reported denials are one-line JSON objects with a
fixed
.Va kind
and stable
.Va code .
Failures and completed denials are written to standard error; the sandboxed
program may also write there.
The trap kinds are:
.Bl -tag -width filesystem
.It Va filesystem
A denied read or write, with code
.Va FILESYSTEM_DENIED .
.It Va network
A denied connect or bind, with code
.Va NETWORK_DENIED .
.It Va launch
The sandbox was installed but the program did not start, with code
.Va LAUNCH_FAILED .
.It Va usage
The command line was rejected, with code
.Va USAGE_ERROR .
.It Va internal
A failure before the program ran.
The code identifies the failed stage, such as
.Va POLICY_PARSE_FAILED
or
.Va SANDBOX_SETUP_FAILED .
.El
.Pp
On Linux, a socket passed with
.Fl -trap-fd
may receive a filesystem or network trap whose
.Va state
is
.Va query
while the operation waits for an integrating host.
Query traps go only to that socket.
Kernel-only and static-profile denials do not always produce a per-access trap.
Writes to the trap descriptor are best effort.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Cm run
returns the sandboxed program's exit status.
.Cm policy validate
returns 1 when its report marks the policy invalid.
.Cm doctor
and
.Cm windows status
return 1 when their report is unhealthy.
Other Landstrip failures return 1, and usage errors return 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run tests with a JSON policy:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
landstrip run -p policy.json -- cargo test
.Ed
.Pp
Validate a YAML policy from standard input:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cat policy.yaml | landstrip policy validate -p - --policy-format yaml
.Ed
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Jarkko Sakkinen Aq Mt jarkko.sakkinen@iki.fi
